# Readability and Simple Ordering

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M3 Story/sticker readability locally revalidated; user/native acceptance pending
Dependencies: 04_VISUAL_DESIGN.todo, 05_WEBSITE_AND_ORDERING.todo, 06_TESTING_AND_LAUNCH.todo

## Purpose

Make the bakery usable by customers with varied reading needs and digital
confidence. The user explicitly prioritizes font sizes, accessible presentation
and intuitive use over decorative detail. The earlier three-section reduction was
implemented, then superseded by the user's explicit story restoration. Workstream
09 owns home -> story -> cakes -> order and transparent cake stickers; the readable
text/direct-order baseline remains and the current local review has passed.
Completed earlier checks remain historical, separate from the current results.

## Tasks

- [x] Record the audience requirement without treating age as a proxy for ability.
- [x] Study Bakingo and Creme Castle desktop/mobile layouts and the four supplied images.
- [x] Preserve the references separately from public bakery assets.
- [x] Increase ordinary copy to 18px and important labels/help to at least 16px.
- [x] Keep principal buttons/navigation targets at least 48px high.
- [x] Make the main mobile navigation visible without a hamburger interaction.
- [x] Use plain labels: View cakes, How to order and Ask about this cake.
- [x] Complete the earlier three-section reduction; its story exclusion is now
  superseded by 09, while FAQs, extra custom-cake content and forms stay out.
- [x] Show all five real cakes with short design names and appearance-based categories.
- [x] Make cake and ordering actions direct links, with no form or clipboard step.
- [x] Keep the earlier revision concise without shrinking type.
- [x] Recheck current readable copy/layout bounds in 09 without imposing the
  obsolete three-section 180-word cap or removing the approved story.
- [x] Explain the Instagram handoff and possible login; do not imply prefilled DMs.
- [x] Label photo enlargement and Close/Previous/Next controls in visible text.
- [x] Preserve contrast, focus visibility, original photo framing and reduced motion.
- [x] Review narrow screens and 200% text resizing.
- [ ] Activate a confirmed public WhatsApp number when supplied.
- [ ] Consider click-to-call only after a public number/contact preference is confirmed.
- [ ] Gather representative-customer feedback on finding a cake and contacting the baker.
- [ ] Complete real-device and native assistive-technology acceptance.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Customers can reach direct contact without discovering or completing a form.
- [x] The earlier three-section scope was implemented and preserved as history.
- [x] Revalidate four-section story/sticker local accessibility checks under workstream 09.
- [x] Key information is not dependent on tiny text, icons, hover or carousel gestures.
- [x] Enlarged text does not force horizontal page scrolling in the reviewed layout.
- [x] The actual cake remains visible; the enlargement label sits below its image.
- [ ] Representative users can complete the intended task without coaching.

## Completion evidence

- Requirements: ..\AGENTS.md and ..\docs\layout-reference-review.md.
- Implementation: ..\web\readability.css, index.template.html and main.mjs.
- Earlier three-section output/review: ..\.local\revisions\before-stickers-20261004\.
  That revision had 33 public files and 19 passing Node cases, with actual
  desktop/mobile/200% text views inspected.
- Current build is 66 files. Workstream 12 and ..\.local\website-review\review.json
  record passed browser/text/control checks across six widths, no-JS, keyboard/
  dialog, 200% text and slow-network loading. Main DOM copy is 188 words (113 focus
  + 75 story); labels remain 16px+ and controls 48px+. Parent inspected desktop/
  mobile full pages and the 200% order screenshot. User/native acceptance is open.
- The repository-memory service did not accept a repository-scoped entry.
  The requirement is preserved in project instructions and this TODO instead;
  no global-memory success is claimed.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-04 - Completed current local readability regression review for the restored
  story/stickers: six widths, 16px+ key labels, 48px controls, keyboard/no-JS and
  200% text pass. Parent inspected actual page views. Workstream 09 records local
  completion separately from representative-user/native-device/AT acceptance.
- 2026-10-04 - Preserved 18px reading copy, 16px key labels, 48px principal controls
  and direct contact while restoring the original story and adding white-contour
  stickers. Workstream 09 supersedes only the former story exclusion/three-section
  boundary; current local revalidation remains in progress.
- 2026-10-04 - User requested less text and a three-section focus. Reduced main DOM
  copy to 115 words, retained large text and all five cakes, and removed the helper
  rather than making it another step. Long-page state is archived before this edit.
- 2026-10-04 - User supplied two live sites/four visual references and emphasized
  readable, accessible, intuitive presentation. Completed the studies and applied
  the readability/direct-contact refinement while preserving the earlier prototype.
